  ('68cf02bf-e822-598d-b657-2d79fb136aed', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g2-argument-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Listen. A mountain is an exciting place to visit. You can hike on winding trails and climb up high. From the top, you can see for miles and miles in every direction. On some tall mountains, there is snow even in the middle of summer. You might also spot goats that climb on the rocks. Which reason supports the point that a mountain is exciting to visit? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"You can see far.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"You can see far."}},{"text":"It is quiet.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It is quiet."}},{"text":"You can fish.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"You can fish."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$You can see far.$q$, $q$A mountain may be quiet, and you might fish in a mountain lake, but the author does not say so. One reason given is that from the top you can see for miles.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
