   $q$Listen. A pencil is the best tool for math. With a pencil, you can erase a mistake and try again. Pencil lines are thin, so your numbers stay neat. Crayons are the best tool for art. Crayons come in many bright colors, and they are fun to color with on big paper. The author says you can erase a mistake. Which point does that reason support? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"Pencil for math.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Pencil for math."}},{"text":"Crayons for art.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Crayons for art."}},{"text":"Pens for notes.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Pens for notes."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Pencil for math.$q$, $q$Erasing a mistake is a reason that a pencil is best for math. Bright colors are a reason that crayons are best for art.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
