   $q$Listen. Board games are good for families. Playing a game gets everyone talking and laughing together at the table. Many games help kids practice counting and reading. Games also teach you how to take turns and be a good sport, even when you lose. Some families pick one night each week for game night. Which reason supports the point that board games are good for families? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"They help you count.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"They help you count."}},{"text":"They are quick.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"They are quick."}},{"text":"They have dice.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"They have dice."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They help you count.$q$, $q$Some games have dice, but that is not a reason the author gives. One reason is that many games help kids practice counting and reading.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
