  ('1349b221-6db4-550b-bd28-5e27eea3356b', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g2-argument-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Listen. Butterflies are amazing insects. A butterfly starts its life as a tiny caterpillar that eats lots of leaves. Later it makes a hard case around itself and changes inside it. Then it comes out with brand new wings. Some butterflies fly thousands of miles each fall to reach a warmer place. Which is NOT a reason the author gives? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"They change shape.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"They change shape."}},{"text":"They are pretty.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"They are pretty."}},{"text":"Some fly far.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Some fly far."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They are pretty.$q$, $q$Many people think butterflies are pretty, but the author does not say so. The reasons are that a caterpillar changes into a butterfly, and some butterflies fly very far.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
