  ('ee44a169-8c6d-5f36-b8d1-6615fe0660d5', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g2-argument-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Listen. It is important to brush your teeth two times a day. Brushing cleans away bits of food that get stuck on your teeth. It helps stop holes in your teeth, called cavities, from forming. Brushing also keeps your breath fresh, so you can smile and talk up close. Many dentists say to brush for two minutes. Which reason supports the point that brushing your teeth is important? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"It wakes you up.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It wakes you up."}},{"text":"It stops cavities.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It stops cavities."}},{"text":"It makes teeth grow.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It makes teeth grow."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It stops cavities.$q$, $q$The author says brushing is important. One reason is that brushing helps stop holes in your teeth, called cavities. It also keeps your breath fresh.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
