  ('16caa09c-38b8-59bf-8cab-0c35520ea827', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g2-argument-evidence'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Listen. Learning about space is exciting. You can find out why the moon seems to change shape during the month. You can learn the names of planets, like Mars and Jupiter. You can look at stars through a telescope at night. Some kids may even grow up to fly on a rocket. Which is NOT a reason the author gives? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"Study the moon.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Study the moon."}},{"text":"See dinosaurs.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"See dinosaurs."}},{"text":"Learn planet names.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Learn planet names."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$See dinosaurs.$q$, $q$Dinosaurs are not part of this text. The reasons are that you can learn about the moon, learn planet names, and maybe one day fly on a rocket.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
