  ('d864c3bd-9999-5728-b2cd-1bb3a0342ece', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g2-argument-evidence'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Listen. Our town should build a new playground. The old one has broken swings and a cracked slide that could hurt someone. Kids need a safe place to climb, swing, and run. A playground is also a place where families can meet and make friends. The old one was built a very long time ago. Which reason would also support the author's point? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"Slides are tall.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Slides are tall."}},{"text":"The old one is fun.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"The old one is fun."}},{"text":"Room for more kids.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Room for more kids."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Room for more kids.$q$, $q$The author wants a new playground. A new playground with room for more kids is one more reason to build it. Saying the old one is fun would not help the point.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
