   $q$Listen. Kids should play outside every day. Fresh air and sunshine help many kids feel good. Running, climbing, and jumping help make muscles and bones grow strong. Outside, kids can find bugs, leaves, and rocks to learn about. Playing outside with friends can also help kids learn to share and get along. Which reason would also support the author's point? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"It can be cold.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It can be cold."}},{"text":"Screens are bright.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Screens are bright."}},{"text":"Kids sleep better.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Kids sleep better."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Kids sleep better.$q$, $q$Many kids sleep better after a day of active play, so that reason fits the point. Cold weather is a reason to stay in, not to go out.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
