   $q$Listen. A camel is well made for the hot, dry desert. Its wide feet help it walk on soft sand without sinking. Long eyelashes help keep blowing sand out of its eyes. A camel can go a long time without drinking water. Its hump stores fat, which gives it energy when food is hard to find. Which reason would also support the author's point? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"It likes snow.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It likes snow."}},{"text":"It can carry people.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It can carry people."}},{"text":"It closes its nose.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It closes its nose."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It closes its nose.$q$, $q$A camel can close its nose to keep out blowing sand, so that fits the point about the desert. Carrying people does not show how a camel lives in the desert.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
