   $q$Listen. Leo wants the class to visit the aquarium, because the class is learning about sea animals. Ana wants the class to visit the apple orchard, because kids can pick fruit and see how apples grow. Both trips are close to school, and both are fun. The class will vote on Friday. The author says the class is learning about sea animals. Which point does that reason support? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"Go to the aquarium.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Go to the aquarium."}},{"text":"Stay at school.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Stay at school."}},{"text":"Go to the orchard.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Go to the orchard."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Go to the aquarium.$q$, $q$Leo wants to go to the aquarium because the class is learning about sea animals. Ana's reason for the orchard is picking fruit and seeing how apples grow.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
